# {{.Project.Name}}

A Go web service generated by [gobento](https://github.com/Tales-of-zuna/gobento).

## Run

```sh
go run ./{{.Slots.entry.Dir}}
```

The server listens on port 8080; set `PORT` to change it. It connects to the
database named by `DATABASE_URL`, as described in [Database](#database).

```sh
curl localhost:8080/health
curl -X POST localhost:8080/items -d '{"name":"first"}'
curl localhost:8080/items
```

## Test

```sh
go test ./...
```

## Layout

| Directory | Contents |
|---|---|
| `{{.Slots.entry.Dir}}` | Entry point: configuration and wiring |
| `{{.Slots.models.Dir}}` | Data types and the interfaces between packages |
| `{{.Slots.handlers.Dir}}` | HTTP handlers |
| `{{.Slots.database.Dir}}` | Database connection and schema |
| `{{.Slots.store.Dir}}` | Data access, implementing the model interfaces |
